      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(anthropic): seed API-key default models using own entries",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nAnthropic API-key model defaulting used prototype-sensitive model-map membership when deciding whether an allowlisted model ref already existed. If process-global prototype state contains one of those refs, default seeding can skip or mishandle the canonical own model entry.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nUse own-property checks before skipping allowlist seeding, and create missing allowlist entries with a descriptor-safe own-property write. Existing own model entries are still preserved, inherited prototype refs no longer block the canonical default entry, and inherited non-writable/getter/setter descriptors cannot throw or intercept the write.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAPI-key Anthropic profiles get the expected own default model entries even when process-global prototype state contains an allowlisted model ref. Existing own model config remains unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact head: `b74260a657c6fdeacf726f76bdb54c08835a5049`\n\nBehavior covered by `extensions/anthropic/config-defaults.own-entries.test.ts`:\n\n- inherited writable data descriptor: writes an own `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5` entry with `cacheRetention: \"short\"`;\n- inherited non-writable data descriptor: still writes the own entry without throwing;\n- inherited getter-only accessor: still writes the own entry without throwing;\n- inherited setter accessor: writes the own entry without invoking the inherited setter;\n- existing own model config is preserved;\n- the prior `Object.prototype` descriptor is restored in `finally`.\n\nThis replaces the earlier custom-prototype test, which was not a valid base/head regression because `{ ...defaults.models }` discards that custom prototype before the changed check runs.\n\nReal setup proof through the core provider-policy seam:\n\n```text\nsurface=applyProviderConfigDefaultsForConfig provider=anthropic\nownEntry=true\nsetterCalled=false\ncacheRetention=short\ndescriptor={\"configurable\":true,\"enumerable\":true,\"writable\":true}\n```\n\nValidation run:\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/anthropic/config-defaults.own-entries.test.ts` (4 tests passed)\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check --threads=1 extensions/anthropic/config-defaults.ts extensions/anthropic/config-defaults.own-entries.test.ts`\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxlint --threads=1 extensions/anthropic/config-defaults.ts extensions/anthropic/config-defaults.own-entries.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.extensions.test.json --incremental false --pretty false`\n- `node --import tsx --input-type=module` proof using `applyProviderConfigDefaultsForConfig({ provider: \"anthropic\", ... })`\n- `env -u OPENAI_API_KEY -u OPENAI_ORG_ID -u OPENAI_PROJECT_ID .agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local` (exit 0, no findings)\n",
        "branch": "alix/anthropic-api-key-own-default-models",
